[Chapter "Early queen moves"]
[Line "The b7 trick after 3.Nc3 and e3"]
[Opening "Slav Defense"]

{A trap every Slav player meets: once the bishop leaves c8, b7 can be attacked.} 1. d4 d5 {Claim the centre.} 2. c4 {The Queen's Gambit: White attacks d5.} 2... c6 {The Slav: support d5 with a pawn and keep the c8 bishop's diagonal open, unlike ...e6.} 3. Nc3 Nf6 {Develop.} 4. e3 Bf5 {Bishop out first, as usual.} 5. cxd5 cxd5 {Recapture with the pawn.} 6. Qb3 {The trick: White hits b7, which the bishop no longer defends.} 6... Bc8 {The simplest answer: the bishop goes back to guard b7. Black has lost some time, but the position is solid.} *
